      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s tricky to tell what might go wrong if we remove these codepoints from paths - how paths may get treated differently in unanticipated ways that could actually grant extra access, or leave openings, rather than restricting access.\n\nFor this reason, I want to try changing the approach to simply reject dealing with paths that have such codepoints, with the goal being to react to such operations with \"permission denied\" / \"access denied\", or perhaps in the case of directory listings, to return no contents.",
      "revId": "21f74da80327dc399a4ad350dbc886248e5736d1",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
