      "writtenOn": "2025-02-23T19:27:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve now done this for PS3, but:\n- Paths are *still* probe-able when ignorable codepoints are included, because \"No such file or directory\" is shown when files truly doesn\u0027t exist, with our error/exception not even being logged, whereas \"Operation not permitted\" is shown when we do catch and handle these codepoints.\n- `stat` also still works on paths containing ignorable codepoints.\n- As commented elsewhere in this relation chain, this might be unavoidable without further hooks in FuseDaemon. Not sure.",
